For that, we create a helper function which takes two nodes as arguments, and checks whether they are symmetric or not. The base case is reached when both nodes are null, and they are obviously symmetric.

Then for each pair of nodes, we check whether their values are the same and whether their left and right subtrees are symmetric or not.

Here is the Python code for this approach:

```
def isSymmetric(root):
    def helper(p, q):
        if not p and not q:
            return True
        if not p or not q:
            return False
        return p.val == q.val and helper(p.left, q.right) and helper(p.right, q.left)
    return helper(root, root)
```

